{"before": "Niraselya Leafshade and Godgiva Greyfell reached the house in Marlmarch at dusk. Secile, the hot-headed sailor, stood in the doorway with her guests behind her. Bormir, the mud-splashed potter, kept to the hearth. The doors were shut and knives showed. Gaddan, the peddler, waited in the lane.", "after": "Niraselya laughed and began to talk. She praised the bread, then the knives, then the sailors' manners, and she kept it up until the guests did not know where to look. Secile snapped at her to hush. Her eyes went to the empty chair by the hearth.

Godgiva saw it and crossed the room. Under the cushion she found Gaddan's locket and a sealed paper. Bormir said nothing and stepped aside. Secile's guests lowered their knives.

Godgiva carried both out to the lane. Gaddan took the locket in his hand and held it a long while.", "summary": "The company found the stolen locket and sealed paper in the sailor's house in Marlmarch, and the peddler Gaddan has them back."}
